    "body": "## Description\n\nThis pull request adds canonical method-aware quote lifecycle support and reusable NUT-30 onchain mint quotes. It makes BOLT11 mint preparation quote-first, adds reusable onchain quote creation and balance-gated withdrawal finalization, and persists canonical mint/melt quote records across the storage adapters.\n\n## Problem\n\nMint quote state was previously tied to operation-shaped snapshots, which made quote-level observation, reusable address quotes, sibling operation lookup, and adapter persistence ambiguous. NUT-30 onchain minting also needs durable NUT-20 quote keys and canonical quote balance tracking so funded reusable quotes can be claimed safely without double-spending locally executing siblings.\n\n## Summary\n\n- Adds `QuoteApi`, canonical quote lifecycle persistence, method-scoped mint quote data, quote-level `mint-quote:updated` events, and reusable onchain mint handling.\n- Adds NUT-20 mint quote key purpose metadata plus deterministic onchain withdrawal preparation/finalization and auto-claim processing for funded reusable quotes.\n- Updates SQLite3, SQLite Bun, Expo SQLite, IndexedDB, and memory repositories for canonical mint/melt quotes, legacy quote snapshot migration, and adapter contract coverage.\n- Updates docs and integration coverage for quote-first minting and NUT-30 onchain mint flows.\n- Compatibility risk: this changes released core APIs/events, persistent adapter schemas, and mint quote protocol behavior; changesets mark the affected packages accordingly.\n\n## Verification\n\n- `bun run --filter='@cashu/coco-core' test:unit`\n- `./scripts/test-integration.sh sqlite-bun`\n\n## Changeset\n\n- Added `.changeset/quote-first-bolt11.md` for major quote-first/canonical quote storage changes across core and adapters.\n- Added `.changeset/decoupled-mint-quotes.md`, `.changeset/remote-quote-fetch.md`, `.changeset/silver-onchain-claims.md`, `.changeset/smart-quote-watchers.md`, and `.changeset/bright-onchain-mints.md` for follow-up core API/event/onchain behavior updates.",
